dashboard.definition:
{
	"title": "IT - Critical Systems Health",
	"description": "Network health, device status, compliance, inventory, and configuration",
	"inputs": {
		"input_global_trp": {
			"options": {
				"defaultValue": "-4h@m,now",
				"token": "global_time"
			},
			"title": "",
			"type": "input.timerange"
		}
	},
	"defaults": {
		"dataSources": {
			"ds.search": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			},
			"ds.spl2": {
				"options": {
					"queryParameters": {
						"earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
						"latest": "$global_time.latest$"
					}
				}
			}
		},
		"tokens": {
			"default": {}
		}
	},
	"visualizations": {
		"viz_about_bg": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_about_purpose": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontColor": "#2B2B2B",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "# IT — Critical Systems Health\n\nReal-time, centralized view of **critical infrastructure health** across network and core systems. Use this dashboard to assess system status, identify anomalies, and prioritize response to potential service-impacting issues.\n\n**Audience:** Network Operations, Infrastructure Leads, IT Management\n**Primary Sources:** Cisco Catalyst Center (DNAC), Cisco IOS Syslog, Cisco ISE, DHCP Servers\n**Refresh:** All panels follow the global time picker; key saved searches run every 15 minutes\n\n---\n\n## How to Navigate This Dashboard\n\n**Overview** — Health scores, issue counts, syslog severity, device inventory, compliance trends.\n*Start here — confirm the backbone is operating within normal bounds.*\n\n**Details & KPI Reference** — Site-level breakdowns, WAN circuit reference, topology map, full device inventory.\n*Drill in when Overview shows degraded health or rising issue counts.*\n\n**Catalyst Center Intelligence** — Deep DNAC analytics: unreachable devices, CPU/memory alerts, DHCP events, power resilience.\n*Investigation mode — root cause analysis on specific device or site issues.*\n\n> **Reading pattern:** Green numbers on Overview = healthy, move on. Yellow/red = switch to Details for site-level context, then CC Intelligence for device-level root cause."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_about_sources": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontColor": "#2B2B2B",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## Data Sources & Troubleshooting\n\n---\n\n**Cisco Catalyst Center** — Cisco DNA Center App for Splunk\nSourcetypes: `cisco:dnac:networkhealth`, `cisco:dnac:devicehealth`, `cisco:dnac:issues`, `cisco:dnac:compliance`\nFreshness: ~15 min\n\n**Network Syslog** — Splunk Add-on for Cisco ESA / IOS\nSourcetypes: `cisco:ios`, `cisco:asa`\nFreshness: Real-time\n\n**DHCP (Windows)** — Splunk Add-on for Windows\nSourcetypes: `WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Dhcp*`\nFreshness: Real-time\n\n**ITSI KPI Summary** — Splunk ITSI\nSourcetypes: `itsi_summary`\nFreshness: Per-service interval\n\n---\n\n**Panel showing \"No results\"?**\n\n1. **Widen the time range** — some metrics need 4+ hours of data to populate\n2. **Verify the TAs are installed** — check *Manage Apps* for the add-ons listed above\n3. **Confirm data flow** — run `index=* sourcetype=cisco:dnac:* | head 5` to test\n4. **Check saved search status** — some panels depend on scheduled searches; verify they are enabled under *Settings → Searches, Reports, and Alerts*."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_ap_loc_bar": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_ap_by_location"
			},
			"description": "Access points per site",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"dataValuesDisplay": "all",
				"legendDisplay": "off",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleVisibility": "hide"
			},
			"title": "AP Count by Location",
			"type": "splunk.bar"
		},
		"viz_box_analysis": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_counts": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_device_table": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_issues": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_maps": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_row1": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_row2": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_box_row3": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_charts": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_compliance": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_dhcp": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_guest": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_kpi": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_power": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_power_detect": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_power_timeline": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_routing": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_tables1": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_box_tables2": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.78)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.08)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_compliance_report_header": {
			"options": {
				"fontColor": "#049FD9",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "### Non-Compliant Device Report\nDevices failing Catalyst Center compliance checks — RUNNING_CONFIG, IMAGE, PSIRT, EOX"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_cc_compliance_report_table": {
			"context": {
				"viz_cc_compliance_report_table_Manageability_colors": [
					{
						"match": "Unmanaged",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Managed (With Errors)",
						"value": "rgba(229,168,35,0.30)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Managed",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				],
				"viz_cc_compliance_report_table_Reachability_colors": [
					{
						"match": "Unreachable",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Reachable",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_compliance_report"
			},
			"description": "Devices failing compliance checks with detail",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"columnFormat": {
					"Manageability": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"Manageability\") | matchValue(viz_cc_compliance_report_table_Manageability_colors)"
					},
					"Reachability": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"Reachability\") | matchValue(viz_cc_compliance_report_table_Reachability_colors)"
					}
				},
				"count": 20,
				"fontSize": "small",
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"headerBackgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.06)",
					"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(rgba(255,255,255,0.03))"
				}
			},
			"title": "Non-Compliant Devices",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_cc_cpu_mem_table": {
			"context": {
				"viz_cc_cpu_mem_table_cpustatus_colors": [
					{
						"match": "Critical",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Warning",
						"value": "rgba(229,168,35,0.30)"
					},
					{
						"match": "OK",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				],
				"viz_cc_cpu_mem_table_memstatus_colors": [
					{
						"match": "Critical",
						"value": "rgba(214,69,80,0.35)"
					},
					{
						"match": "Warning",
						"value": "rgba(229,168,35,0.30)"
					},
					{
						"match": "OK",
						"value": "rgba(110,190,74,0.15)"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_cpu_mem"
			},
			"description": "Devices with CPU or memory utilization > 80%",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"columnFormat": {
					"cpu_status": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"cpu_status\") | matchValue(viz_cc_cpu_mem_table_cpustatus_colors)"
					},
					"mem_status": {
						"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"mem_status\") | matchValue(viz_cc_cpu_mem_table_memstatus_colors)"
					}
				},
				"count": 10,
				"fontSize": "small",
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(rowBackgroundColorsByIndex)"
				}
			},
			"title": "CPU / Memory Threshold Alerts",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_cc_dhcp_table": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_dhcp_events"
			},
			"description": "Pool exhaustion, lease denial, and range events from Windows DHCP",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"count": 10,
				"fontSize": "small",
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(rowBackgroundColorsByIndex)"
				}
			},
			"title": "DHCP Pool Events",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_cc_header_bg": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.88)",
				"rx": 10,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.06)"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cc_health_dist_bar": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_health_dist"
			},
			"description": "By device family and site — Good (8-10), Fair (5-7), Poor (1-4)",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"dataValuesDisplay": "all",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#6EBE4A",
					"#E5A823",
					"#D64550",
					"#6E6E6E"
				],
				"stackMode": "stacked",
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleVisibility": "hide"
			},
			"title": "Device Health Score Distribution",
			"type": "splunk.bar"
		},
		"viz_cc_info": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontColor": "#2B2B2B",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## Metric Reference — Catalyst Center Intelligence Tab\n\n---\n\n#### Critical Alerts\n\n**Unreachable Devices** — Devices Catalyst Center cannot reach via SNMP/SSH\n**CPU/Memory Alerts** — Devices with utilization > 80% (Warning) or > 90% (Critical)\n**Recent Reboots** — Devices with uptime < 4 hours (unexpected restarts or maintenance)\n**DHCP Pool Events** — DHCP NACK, denial, and pool exhaustion events from Windows servers\n\n---\n\n#### Health Distribution & Trends\n\n**Device Health Score Distribution** — All devices categorized as Good (8–10), Fair (5–7), Poor (1–4) by family and site\n**Issue Trend by Category** — Hourly timechart of categorized DNAC issues\n**Network Health Trend** — Good / Fair / Bad percentages from Catalyst Center health rollup\n\n---\n\n#### Device Deep-Dive\n\n**Unreachable Devices Table** — Full detail: device name, family, platform, site, IP, failure reason\n**CPU/Memory Threshold Alerts** — Resource-constrained devices with CPU/memory status\n**Top 20 Devices by Issue Count** — Most problematic devices ranked by active issues\n**Issues by Site** — Per-site issue counts with critical/high breakdown\n\n---\n\n#### DHCP & Interface\n\n**DHCP Pool Events** — Pool exhaustion and lease denial events\n**Issues by Priority** — P1–P4 distribution across all DNAC-detected issues\n**Interface Utilization Alerts** — Bandwidth saturation hotspots by device and site\n**Guest Client Count Trend** — Connected client count with capacity threshold lines\n**Recently Rebooted Devices** — Devices rebooted within the monitoring window\n\n---\n\n#### ⚡ Power Event Correlation\n\n**Power Events** — Power-related syslog events (RELOAD, PLATFORM_ENV, SWITCHOVER, STACK_CHANGE)\n**Power Event Timeline** — Chronology: Reload → Link Down → Protocol Down → Reconvergence → Recovery\n**Power Event Detection** — Correlated syslog events classified by type with affected devices\n**Link Flap Storm Detection** — Distinguishes mass power events from isolated port issues\n**Routing Reconvergence** — OSPF/EIGRP/BGP neighbor state changes showing Down → Up recovery\n**STP Reconvergence** — Spanning-tree topology changes per device/VLAN after power events\n**Non-Compliant Devices** — Compliance policy failures from Catalyst Center"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_cc_intf_util_table": {
			"context": {
				"issue_countColumnFormatEditorConfig": {
					"number": {
						"thousandSeparated": true,
						"unitPosition": "after"
					}
				}
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_intf_util"
			},
			"description": "Bandwidth saturation hotspots from DNAC issues",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"columnFormat": {
					"issue_count": {
						"align": "auto",
						"data": "> table | seriesByName(\"issue_count\") | formatByType(issue_countColumnFormatEditorConfig)",
						"headerAlign": "auto",
						"textOverflow": "break-word",
						"width": 90
					}
				},
				"count": 10,
				"fontSize": "small",
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(rowBackgroundColorsByIndex)"
				}
			},
			"title": "Interface Utilization Alerts",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_cc_issue_priority_donut": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_issue_by_priority"
			},
			"description": "P1/P2/P3/P4 distribution",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"labelDisplay": "valuesAndPercentage",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#D64550",
					"#E5A823",
					"#E5A823",
					"#6E6E6E"
				],
				"showDonutHole": true
			},
			"title": "Issues by Priority",
			"type": "splunk.pie"
		},
		"viz_cc_issue_site_table": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_issue_by_site"
			},
			"description": "Issue count per site with severity and affected device count",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"count": 10,
				"fontSize": "small",
				"headerVisibility": "fixed",
				"tableFormat": {
					"rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(rowBackgroundColorsByIndex)"
				}
			},
			"title": "Issues by Site",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_cc_issue_trend_area": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_issue_trend_cat"
			},
			"description": "Categorized DNAC issues over time — correlate spikes with incidents",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"stackMode": "stacked",
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleVisibility": "hide"
			},
			"title": "Issue Trend by Category",
			"type": "splunk.area"
		},
		"viz_cc_kpi_cpu_mem": {
			"context": {
				"trendColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 0,
						"value": "#6E6E6E"
					},
					{
						"from": 0,
						"value": "#6EBE4A"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_kpi_cpu_mem"
			},
			"description": "Devices with CPU or memory utilization above threshold",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#049FD9",
				"majorFontSize": 36,
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"showSparklineAreaGraph": true,
				"showSparklineTooltip": true,
				"showTrendIndicator": true,
				"sparklineAreaColor": "#049FD9",
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#049FD9",
				"trendColor": "> trendValue | rangeValue(trendColorEditorConfig)",
				"trendDisplay": "percent"
			},
			"title": "CPU/Memory Alerts >80%",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_cc_kpi_dhcp": {
			"context": {
				"trendColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 0,
						"value": "#6E6E6E"
					},
					{
						"from": 0,
						"value": "#6EBE4A"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_kpi_dhcp"
			},
			"description": "DHCP pool exhaustion or lease denial events",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#049FD9",
				"majorFontSize": 36,
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"showSparklineAreaGraph": true,
				"showSparklineTooltip": true,
				"showTrendIndicator": true,
				"sparklineAreaColor": "#049FD9",
				"sparklineDisplay": "below",
				"sparklineNullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"sparklineStrokeColor": "#049FD9",
				"trendColor": "> trendValue | rangeValue(trendColorEditorConfig)",
				"trendDisplay": "percent"
			},
			"title": "DHCP Pool Events",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_cc_kpi_power": {
			"context": {
				"majorColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 1,
						"value": "#6EBE4A"
					},
					{
						"from": 1,
						"to": 3,
						"value": "#E5A823"
					},
					{
						"from": 3,
						"value": "#D64550"
					}
				]
			},
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_power_summary_count"
			},
			"description": "Power-related syslog events detected",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"majorColor": "> majorValue | rangeValue(majorColorEditorConfig)",
				"majorFontSize": 42,
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"showTrendIndicator": false,
				"sparklineDisplay": "off"
			},
			"title": "Power Events",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_cc_kpi_reboots": {
			"context": {
				"trendColorEditorConfig": [
					{
						"to": 0,
						"value": "#6E6E6E"
					},
