		"viz_md_config_detail_header": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
				"fontColor": "#000000",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "**Recent human config changes** &mdash; Detailed audit log entries for human-initiated workflows in the selected window. Each row = one action: **who** triggered it (admin), **how** (DNAC UI / API), **what** was done (description with newlines collapsed), and **where** (target site / device / template / network profile). Use this table to drill into individual changes captured in the trend tile above. Source: `cisco:dnac:audit:logs`."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_md_ise_logins_header": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
				"fontColor": "#000000",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "**Identity-attested device logins** &mdash; Cross-source view of who authenticated to network devices via TACACS+/ISE &mdash; including auth success/failure and per-command authorization decisions (allowed / denied) &mdash; and the last device they touched. Pair this with the Catalyst Center audit table above to confirm config changes were performed by an authorized human and not via an out-of-band channel. Source: `cisco:ise:syslog`."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_md_workflow_header": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
				"fontColor": "#000000",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "**Human config workflows** &mdash; A *workflow* = one admin &times; one 5-minute window of activity, collapsing multi-device fan-out (a single push to 28 devices that fires 8 audit lines within 5 min counts as **1 workflow**, not 8). Excludes service accounts, sub-events, read-only commands, and \"Going to deploy\" precursors. Source: `cisco:dnac:audit:logs`."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_narr_cc_intel": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
