				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"legendDisplay": "right",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#6EBE4A",
					"#E5A823",
					"#D64550"
				],
				"stackMode": "stacked100",
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide"
			},
			"title": "Client Health Trend",
			"type": "splunk.area"
		},
		"viz_uxh_dev_types_bar": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_uxh_top_device_types"
			},
			"description": "Top device categories by unique MAC count",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"dataValuesDisplay": "all",
				"legendDisplay": "off",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleVisibility": "hide"
			},
			"title": "Top 5 Device Types",
			"type": "splunk.bar"
		},
		"viz_uxh_narrative": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontColor": "#6E6E6E",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "End-user **client experience** seen from Catalyst Center &mdash; wireless and wired health scores, distribution over time, and what kinds of devices are on the network. Use this tab to confirm clients are healthy and to spot which device categories or operating systems trend with degraded experience. Internet-path metrics (ThousandEyes) appear here once the `Cisco_ThousandEyes.Test_Metrics` data model is installed and accelerated."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_uxh_section": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0.45)",
				"fillOpacity": 1,
				"rx": 12,
				"strokeColor": "rgba(0,0,0,0.06)",
				"strokeOpacity": 0.3,
				"strokeWidth": 1
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_uxh_te_note": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontColor": "#2B2B2B",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "### Internet path metrics (ThousandEyes)\n\nThousandEyes per-test latency, loss, jitter, and HTTP availability panels are **temporarily parked** because the `Cisco_ThousandEyes.Test_Metrics` data model is not installed on this stack. Once the *Cisco ThousandEyes App for Splunk* is installed and the data model is accelerated, these panels will return:\n\n- Internet path composite score (gauge)\n- Per-agent latency / loss / jitter table\n- Per-test result table with status\n- Test-health distribution (donut)\n\nReinstating them requires no SPL changes &mdash; the underlying searches already live in `searchbase.conf` and are filterable in the KPI Picker via the `Requires_Cisco_ThousandEyes_DM` tag."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
